3, 33, 33);">
I filed a Petition for Public Records Order in this matter on July 22, 2026=
. I write to supplement the record with one document received today.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
Section III of the petition addresses the comment entered in OSP CAD event =
SP26097765 at 08:41:32 on March 24, 2026, before the responding unit depart=
ed: &quot;FOR THE FOREST SERVICE // FOLLOWUP INTERVIEW W/ ROBERT WHITE 04-1=
1-1977.&quot; Relief item 6 asks the Department
 to produce the communication by which the information in that event was co=
nveyed to the dispatcher who created it.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
On July 23, 2026, Michele Holman, District Ranger for the Central Coast Ran=
ger District, Siuslaw National Forest, U.S. Forest Service, wrote to me reg=
arding that comment. Her email states, in relevant part:</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
&quot;Regarding the CAD entry stating, 'FOR THE FOREST SERVICE,' I am unsur=
e why that wording appears, as the Forest Service did not initiate the inte=
rview. The agency's involvement was limited to assisting OSP by providing a=
ccess and guiding them to the Siltcoos
 Work Center. This is standard practice, as OSP does not have keys to Fores=
t Service gates, work centers, or other secured facilities. Our law enforce=
ment officer accompanied them solely to facilitate entry and ensure they re=
ached the correct location.&quot;</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
The full email is attached as Exhibit 26 (attached below).</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
I offer this without argument and ask nothing further of the Attorney Gener=
al beyond the relief already requested. The relevance is limited and factua=
l: the federal agency named in the Department's own record has stated in wr=
iting that it did not initiate the
 event, and has described the extent of its involvement as providing access=
. The question of how that characterization came to be entered in the Depar=
tment's dispatch record, and by whom, remains among the categories the peti=
tion asks the Department to address.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto" style=3D"font-family: Aptos, Aptos_MSFontService, -apple-=
system, Roboto, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(3=
3, 33, 33);">
<br>
</div>
